  "interpretation": "For batch=1 latency-bound decode, -sm row shards every layer's matmul across all 8 GPUs, forcing a cross-GPU all-reduce/all-gather every token. That collective sync tax dwarfs the tiny per-token compute, so throughput collapses to ~0.3x despite every GPU showing MORE sm activity. -sm layer (pipeline) only passes the small hidden-state activation across a GPU boundary once per layer, so it keeps the 23.4 tok/s baseline. Row-split's design win is compute-bound work (large-batch or long-prompt prefill), NOT single-stream decode -- which is what this A/B isolates.",
